  "fullContentHtml": "\n<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1 ast-no-date-box\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n\n<p><!-- .entry-header --></p>\n<div class=\"entry-content clear\" style=\"height: auto !important;\">\n<div class=\"post-desc\">\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\"><strong>Short Details :</strong> <a style=\"color: #ff0000;\" href=\"https://upmsp.edu.in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\">Uttar Pradesh Madhyamik Shiksha Parishad (UPMSP)</a> </span>has opened the online registration for the 2026 Compartment and Improvement Examinations for both High School (Class 10) and Intermediate (Class 12) students. Students who participated in the UP Board Exams 2026 and either failed in one or more subjects or wish to improve their scores are eligible to apply. The application window is open from June 06, 2026 to June 27, 2026, and submissions can be made through the official website: upmsp.edu.in. Candidates are advised to go through the detailed information regarding the UP Board Compartment Form 2026 provided below.</span></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-2\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable1\">\n<table style=\"font-size: 16px; font-style: normal; width: 100%;\" width=\"100%\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff0000;\">Uttar Pradesh Madhyamik Shiksha Parishad (UPMSP)</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #008000;\">UP Board 10th / 12th Compartment Online Form 2026</span></h2>\n<h2 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\">Exam Name – UP Board 10th / 12th Annual Board Exam 2026</span></h2>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Important Dates</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">10th High School Annual Exam Between : <b>18 February 2026 to 12 March 2026</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">12th Intermediate Annual Exam Between : <b>18 February 2026 to 12 March 2026</b></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Result :<strong> 23 April 2026 Available Now</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"background-color: #ffff00; font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Improvement/ Compartment</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Form Start :<strong> 06 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Last Date :<strong> 27 June 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Exam Date : <strong>Last Week of July 2026 (Expected)</strong></span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Application Fee</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Class 10th High School : <strong>Rs. 256.50/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Class 12th Intermediate : <strong>Rs. 306/-</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Pay the Exam Fee Through E Challan Fee Mode Only.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><b>Exam Details</b></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>Exam Name : </strong>UP Board Class 10th / 12th Annual Board Exam 2026</span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\"><strong>Exam Conducted By : </strong>Uttar Pradesh Madhyamik Shiksha Parishad (UPMSP) Conducted the Examination of Class 10th / 12th Examination 2026</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>UP Board Class 10th/12th Compartment Online Form 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">The UP Board has declared the results of high school and intermediate on Friday. This time 90.42 percent of the candidates have passed in 10th high school and 80.38 percent in intermediate. Like previous years, this time also more girl students have passed the exam than boys. But now the application for Compartment and Improvement has started for the candidates who are not satisfied with their result in the examination.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>UP Board Class 10th/12th Compartment Online Form 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Students of Class 10 (High School) and Class 12 (Intermediate) under the Uttar Pradesh Madhyamik Shiksha Parishad (UPMSP), Prayagraj, who are dissatisfied with their marks in any subject or with their overall result for the 2026 exams, can apply for Compartment and Improvement. Through this process, the answer sheet of the concerned subject will be re-evaluated, and a revised Compartment and Improvement result will be issued accordingly.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>How To Apply UP Board 10th / 12th Compartment Online Form 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"1051\" data-end=\"1090\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Visit the official UPMSP website: <a style=\"color: #000000;\" href=\"https://upmsp.edu.in\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" data-start=\"34\" data-end=\"70\">upmsp.edu.in</a>.</span></li>\n<li data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1133\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Locate and click on the link for “Improvement Examination” or “Compartment Examination” relevant to your class.</span></li>\n<li data-start=\"1137\" data-end=\"1176\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Log in using your roll number, school code, and date of birth.</span></li>\n<li data-start=\"1180\" data-end=\"1219\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Fill out the application form with accurate details.</span></li>\n<li data-start=\"1223\" data-end=\"1262\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Pay the application fee through the prescribed challan.</span></li>\n<li data-start=\"1266\" data-end=\"1305\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Print the completed application form and the original challan.</span></li>\n<li data-start=\"1309\" data-end=\"1387\"><span class=\"relative -mx-px my-[-0.2rem] rounded px-px py-[0.2rem] transition-colors duration-100 ease-in-out\" style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">Send both documents via registered post to your regional UPMSP office by the specified deadline.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Send to UPMSP UP Board 10th / 12th Compartment Form 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">After completing the online application, students must send a printed copy along with the original challan through registered post to the respective regional UPMSP office by <strong data-start=\"174\" data-end=\"191\" data-is-last-node=\"\">June 27, 2026</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; color: #000000;\">The UPMSP has regional offices in Meerut, Bareilly, Prayagraj, Varanasi, and Gorakhpur.</span></li>\n</ul>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"pd-0\" colspan=\"4\" width=\"100%\">\n<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><strong>Instructions To Send UP Board 10th / 12th Compartment Online Form 2026</strong></span></h3>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">To apply, one must fill out the online application form and obtain a printed copy of the Treasury Challan.</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">It must both be sent by registered post to the board office</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">Any application received by post or courier without prior completion of the online form will be rejected by the board.</span></li>\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-size: 12pt;\">The deadline for sending the application and original challan copy via registered post is June 13th, 2026.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><div class=\"code-block code-block-3\" style=\"margin: 8px 0; clear: both;\">\n\n<!-- SarkariExam Home page -->\n\n</div>\n<p></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<div class=\"newtable2\">\n<table style=\"width: 